    "blocks": [
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "However you create AOP proxies, you can manipulate them BY using the "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "org.springframework.aop.framework.Advised"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " interface. Any AOP proxy can be cast to this interface, no matter which other interfaces it implements. This interface includes the following methods:"
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "context": "dlist",
            "id": null,
            "items": [
              {
                "description": {
                  "blocks": [
                    {
                      "context": "listing",
                      "id": null,
                      "inlines": [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "value": "Advisor[] getAdvisors();\n\nvoid addAdvice(Advice advice) throws AopConfigException;\n\nvoid addAdvice(int pos, Advice advice) throws AopConfigException;\n\nvoid addAdvisor(Advisor advisor) throws AopConfigException;\n\nvoid addAdvisor(int pos, Advisor advisor) throws AopConfigException;\n\nint indexOf(Advisor advisor);\n\nboolean removeAdvisor(Advisor advisor) throws AopConfigException;\n\nvoid removeAdvisor(int index) throws AopConfigException;\n\nboolean replaceAdvisor(Advisor a, Advisor b) throws AopConfigException;\n\nboolean isFrozen();"
                        }
                      ],
                      "language": "java",
                      "roles": [],
                      "title": null
                    }
                  ],
                  "checkbox": null,
                  "inlines": []
                },
                "terms": [
                  [
                    {
                      "kind": "text",
                      "value": "Java"
                    }
                  ]
                ]
              },
              {
                "description": {
                  "blocks": [
                    {
                      "context": "listing",
                      "id": null,
                      "inlines": [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "value": "fun getAdvisors(): Array<Advisor>\n\n@Throws(AopConfigException::class)\nfun addAdvice(advice: Advice)\n\n@Throws(AopConfigException::class)\nfun addAdvice(pos: Int, advice: Advice)\n\n@Throws(AopConfigException::class)\nfun addAdvisor(advisor: Advisor)\n\n@Throws(AopConfigException::class)\nfun addAdvisor(pos: Int, advisor: Advisor)\n\nfun indexOf(advisor: Advisor): Int\n\n@Throws(AopConfigException::class)\nfun removeAdvisor(advisor: Advisor): Boolean\n\n@Throws(AopConfigException::class)\nfun removeAdvisor(index: Int)\n\n@Throws(AopConfigException::class)\nfun replaceAdvisor(a: Advisor, b: Advisor): Boolean\n\nfun isFrozen(): Boolean"
                        }
                      ],
                      "language": "kotlin",
                      "roles": [],
                      "title": null
                    }
                  ],
                  "checkbox": null,
                  "inlines": []
                },
                "terms": [
                  [
                    {
                      "kind": "text",
                      "value": "Kotlin"
                    }
                  ]
                ]
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          }
        ],
        "context": "example",
        "id": null,
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "The "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "getAdvisors()"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " method returns an "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Advisor"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " for every advisor, interceptor, or other advice type that has been added to the factory. If you added an "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Advisor"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": ", the returned advisor at this index is the object that you added. If you added an interceptor or other advice type, Spring wrapped this in an advisor with a pointcut that always returns "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "true"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": ". Thus, if you added a "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "MethodInterceptor"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": ", the advisor returned for this index is a "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "DefaultPointcutAdvisor"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " that returns your "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "MethodInterceptor"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " and a pointcut that matches all classes and methods."
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "The "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "addAdvisor()"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " methods can be used to add any "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Advisor"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": ". Usually, the advisor holding pointcut and advice is the generic "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "DefaultPointcutAdvisor"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": ", which you can use with any advice or pointcut (but not for introductions)."
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "By default, it is possible to add or remove advisors or interceptors even once a proxy has been created. The only restriction is that it is impossible to add or remove an introduction advisor, as existing proxies from the factory do not show the interface change. (You can obtain a new proxy from the factory to avoid this problem.)"
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "The following example shows casting an AOP proxy to the "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Advised"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " interface and examining and manipulating its advice:"
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "context": "dlist",
            "id": null,
            "items": [
              {
                "description": {
                  "blocks": [
                    {
                      "context": "listing",
                      "id": null,
                      "inlines": [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "value": "Advised advised = (Advised) myObject;\nAdvisor[] advisors = advised.getAdvisors();\nint oldAdvisorCount = advisors.length;\nSystem.out.println(oldAdvisorCount + \" advisors\");\n\n// Add an advice like an interceptor without a pointcut\n// Will match all proxied methods\n// Can use for interceptors, before, after returning or throws advice\nadvised.addAdvice(new DebugInterceptor());\n\n// Add selective advice using a pointcut\nadvised.addAdvisor(new DefaultPointcutAdvisor(mySpecialPointcut, myAdvice));\n\nassertEquals(\"Added two advisors\", oldAdvisorCount + 2, advised.getAdvisors().length);"
                        }
                      ],
                      "language": "java",
                      "roles": [],
                      "title": null
                    }
                  ],
                  "checkbox": null,
                  "inlines": []
                },
                "terms": [
                  [
                    {
                      "kind": "text",
                      "value": "Java"
                    }
                  ]
                ]
              },
              {
                "description": {
                  "blocks": [
                    {
                      "context": "listing",
                      "id": null,
                      "inlines": [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "value": "val advised = myObject as Advised\nval advisors = advised.advisors\nval oldAdvisorCount = advisors.size\nprintln(\"$oldAdvisorCount advisors\")\n\n// Add an advice like an interceptor without a pointcut\n// Will match all proxied methods\n// Can use for interceptors, before, after returning or throws advice\nadvised.addAdvice(DebugInterceptor())\n\n// Add selective advice using a pointcut\nadvised.addAdvisor(DefaultPointcutAdvisor(mySpecialPointcut, myAdvice))\n\nassertEquals(\"Added two advisors\", oldAdvisorCount + 2, advised.advisors.size)"
                        }
                      ],
                      "language": "kotlin",
                      "roles": [],
                      "title": null
                    }
                  ],
                  "checkbox": null,
                  "inlines": []
                },
                "terms": [
                  [
                    {
                      "kind": "text",
                      "value": "Kotlin"
                    }
                  ]
                ]
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          }
        ],
        "context": "example",
        "id": null,
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "admonition",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "It is questionable whether it is advisable (no pun intended) to modify advice on a business object in production, although there are, no doubt, legitimate usage cases. However, it can be very useful in development (for example, in tests). We have sometimes found it very useful to be able to add test code in the form of an interceptor or other advice, getting inside a method invocation that we want to test. (For example, the advice can get inside a transaction created for that method, perhaps to run SQL to check that a database was correctly updated, before marking the transaction for roll back.)"
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null,
        "type": "note"
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "Depending on how you created the proxy, you can usually set a "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "frozen"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " flag. In that case, the "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Advised"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "isFrozen()"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " method returns "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "true"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": ", and any attempts to modify advice through addition or removal results in an "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "AopConfigException"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": ". The ability to freeze the state of an advised object is useful in some cases (for example, to prevent calling code removing a security interceptor)."
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      }
    ],
    "outline": null,
    "title": [
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "value": "Manipulating Advised Objects"
      }
    ]
  }
}
